---
import Layout from './Layout.astro';
import Topology from './Topology.astro';
import { simple } from './topologies';
---
<Layout title="Simple topology" specimen="simple">
  <article class="ux-topology-page">
    <header><p class="ux-kicker">Specimen 02 · Simple topology</p><h1>Labels that belong.</h1><p class="ux-deck">Devices below their icons. Interfaces beside their endpoints. No decorative numbering.</p><p class="ux-fixture-note">Synthetic geometry for visual review, not a networking lesson.</p></header>
    <Topology topology={simple}/>
    <aside class="ux-design-note"><h2>Read ownership before detail.</h2><p>Hover or keyboard-focus <strong>Gi1/0/7</strong> to connect the reference to its switch, endpoint and client path. On touch, tap the reference; Clear focus restores the default. The labels and connection details remain understandable without interaction.</p></aside>
  </article>
</Layout>
